@startuml exp3_class
title Experiment 3 - C4 code level: classes and functions
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class "main()" as Main <<function>> {
  +main(argc, argv) : int
  reads CPUs, default 2 and 4
  prints measurement and checks
}

class FetchAddCounter <<counter>> {
  +kName : const char*  = "fetch_add"
  +increment() : uint64
  +value() : uint64
  +reset()
  -v_ : atomic uint64
}

class "measure~C~()" as Measure <<function>> {
  +measure(counters, cpus, iterations) : Measurement
  runs 1 warmup race, then 11 timed races
}

class "shared_by()" as Shared <<function>> {
  +shared_by(counter, n) : vector of C*
  n pointers to ONE counter
}

class Measurement <<struct>> {
  +slowest : TrialStats
  +aggregate_mops : TrialStats
  +voluntary_switches_per_trial : double
  +kernel_fraction : double
  +ok() : bool
}

class RaceResult <<struct>> {
  +slowest_ns_per_increment : double
  +observed_total : uint64
  +counts_ok() : bool
}

class "race~C~()" as Race <<function>> {
  +race(counters, cpus, iterations) : RaceResult
  start barrier, pin, time, join, sum
}

Main ..> FetchAddCounter : creates one
Main ..> Shared : calls with 2 threads
Main ..> Measure : calls
Measure ..> Race : calls per trial
Measure ..> Measurement : returns
Race ..> RaceResult : returns
Race ..> FetchAddCounter : calls increment() on each thread

note right of FetchAddCounter
  increment() = one lock add instruction.
  No lock object, no syscall, no sleeping thread.
end note
@enduml
